lomatic  solution to this situation but it does  make diplomatic efforts official  diplomatic efforts more and more  difficult especially from a german  perspective because it gives the  impression to the outside world that  germany is not only  one position that is not working on a  united front that you have on the one  hand the german government and on the  other hand gerhard schroeder former  german chancellor between 1998 and 2005  who has been indeed very criticized by  his closeness to the kremlin and by his  job as a gas lobbyist for  russian energy giants and it's important  to stress that this visit by gerhart was  not coordinated with the current german  government from his perspective from  gerhard schroeder's perspective i  understand or at least i believe this  would be an attempt on his side to try  and polish his image a little bit try  and clean up that image that has been  very criticized because he has refused  so far to drop to cancel those  appointments that he has  with those energy giants from russia so  a very difficult situation all together  from the german perspective because it  makes official negotiations much more  difficult than expected our political  correspondent thomas barrow thanks so  much for joining me in the studio with  that update

